ource_handle\": \"P0177\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Modulation of the response to immunotherapy in triple-negative breast cancer: the role of the microbiota and microbial metabolites in the tumor microenvironment\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦三阴性乳腺癌，确认 Akkermansia、双歧杆菌及高多样性与 ICI/化疗响应相关，详述 TMAO/IPA 增强 CD8+ T 细胞活性、SCFAs 表观遗传调节及瘤内细菌直接作用的机制。指出污染风险及因果不确定性，用于提供高免疫原性肿瘤中微生物调节的特异性证据及方法学警示。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome as an actionable drug-sensitivity modulator for immune checkpoint blockade: clinical evidence for FMT, live biotherapeutics, and defined consortia\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"对比 FMT、LBPs 及定义菌群三类干预的临床证据，指出 FMT 在难治性黑色素瘤中的概念验证效力及 SER-401 试验因抗生素预处理失败的教训。阐述 DC 激活、SCFA 调节及屏障完整性机制，用于构建“生态药理学”框架，解释干预效果差异及基线生态/共用药的关键影响。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0179\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbial structural variation associates with immune checkpoint inhibitor response\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"发现 Akkermansia 等关键菌种的结构变异（SVs）独立于物种丰度与 ICI 疗效相关，提出 SV 区域富集糖代谢酶及免疫调节基因（如α-唾液酸酶）的机制假设。用于论证微生物遗传多样性（亚基因组水平）作为新型生物标志物的价值，并指出从相关性向功能验证过渡的方法学需求。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0180\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome–bile acid-FXR interplay: a pivotal axis in metabolic and gastrointestinal diseases\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述微生物胆汁酸（3-oxo-LCA, isoalloLCA）通过抑制 RORγt 或促进 Treg 分化调节 Th17/Treg 平衡的分子机制，及 FXR/TGR5 在巨噬细胞中的作用。虽聚焦代谢病，但提供微生物代谢物精细调节免疫细胞表型的通用原则，用于类比解释胆汁酸轴在肿瘤免疫微环境中潜在的调节作用及屏障功能的重要性。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to route a batch of 60 sources (P0121-P0180) to a shared outline for a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\"\n\nThe shared outline has 5 chapters:\n- CH01: Clinical evidence landscape (antibiotics, FMT trials, observational data)\n- CH02: Microbial features (predictive taxa and metabolites)\n- CH03: Mechanistic pathways (immune, metabolic, barrier)\n- CH04: Therapeutic interventions (FMT, probiotics, diet feasibility)\n- CH05: Limitations, heterogeneity, translational directions\n\nI need to read each source's B_review_planning card and assign it to appropriate chapter(s) based on its actual content, research type, object, conditions, and depth. I must write specific_usable_material in Chinese (80-150 characters) for each source, indicating what specific facts or comparison angles are usable and their purpose in this review.\n\nLet me go through each source systematically:\n\nP0121: HCC patients, 16S sequencing, Faecalibacterium (beneficial) vs Bacteroidales (detrimental) associated with PFS. Observational, retrospective, HCC-specific. → CH01 (clinical evidence), CH02 (microbial features)\n\nP0122: MET4 bacterial consortium trial, IgG responses, immune remodeling. Phase I/II, safety/colonization not efficacy. → CH03 (mechanisms - immune response), CH04 (interventions - live biotherapeutics)\n\nP0123: NSCLC, metagenomics, taxonomic vs metabolic pathways, PD-L1 status. Observational, Caucasian cohort. → CH01 (clinical evidence), CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms - metabolic pathways)\n\nP0124: 2026 review on microbiome-host axis, mechanisms (inosine, SCFAs), intratumoral microbes. \n\nNarrative review. → CH03 (mechanisms), CH05 (limitations/heterogeneity)\n\nP0125: MRx0518 Phase I/II abstract, ICI-refractory patients. No efficacy data yet. → CH04 (interventions - live biotherapeutics), CH05 (limitations)\n\nP0126: 2021 review on microbiome and toxicity to immune agonist antibodies. MyD88 pathway, preclinical. → CH03 (mechanisms - toxicity pathways), CH05 (limitations - preclinical vs clinical)\n\nP0127: MSI/dMMR pancreatic adenocarcinoma, ICI efficacy clinical data. No microbiome data. → CH01 (clinical evidence - ICI efficacy context), CH05 (limitations - no microbiome data)\n\nP0128: 2026 Nature Reviews Microbiology abstract, microbiome for cancer therapy. Overview framework. → CH03 (mechanisms framework), CH05 (limitations)\n\nP0129: 2020 systematic review, Firmicutes beneficial, Proteobacteria detrimental, antibiotic timing. → CH01 (clinical evidence - antibiotics), CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms - SCFAs)\n\nP0130: 2018 review, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia, mechanisms (DC activation, T cells). → CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms)\n\nP0131: 2021 narrative review, baseline composition, dysbiosis, antibiotics. → CH01 (clinical evidence), CH05 (limitations)\n\nP0132: 2022 review on human microbiome medical applications, Roseburia, cGAS/STING, engineered bacteria. → CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions - engineered bacteria)\n\nP0133: 2024 review on predictive biomarkers and resistance, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, metabolites. → CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms), CH05 (limitations)\n\nP0134: 2023 NSCLC, longitudinal microbiome changes during ICI, small sample (N=5). → CH01 (clinical evidence - longitudinal), CH02 (microbial features - dynamics)\n\nP0135: 2025 meta-analysis on PPI use and ICI outcomes, OS HR=1.18. Observational. → CH01 (clinical evidence - confounding medications), CH03 (mechanisms - Tregs)\n\nP0136: 2024 review on gut microbiota influences ICI efficiency, Akkermansia, SCFAs, FMT. → CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions)\n\nP0137: 2024 NSCLC metatranscriptomics, transcriptional activity vs abundance, Actinobacteria/Archaea in short PFS. → CH02 (microbi